{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789321319,"nonce":"LkhDNGLjF46uhkWSiPKChqrxz2s=","title":"OSR copied a by-reference aggregate into the frame, so a resumed loop mutated a copy of the list header","message":"Reproducer (Python frontend, any tier-0 loop long enough to be promoted while running):\n\n    xs = list(range(600000))\n    print(len(xs), xs[599999])\n\nprints `600000 75711`, or `600000 0`, or segfaults, depending on n. Correct with `ZYNTAX_DISABLE_OSR=1`. The loop that is promoted is `zb_list_extend_i64` (`list(xs)` extends an empty list); its live-ins include the destination list `xs`, whose HIR type is the three-field `List` struct.\n\n`osr::is_held_by_reference` said a multi-field struct is held as a pointer to its storage, and the frame writer (`emit_osr_frame_store`) therefore copied the pointee's 24 bytes into the frame; the helper prologue took the frame slot's address as the value. The helper's pushes then wrote the reallocated data pointer into the frame copy of the header, while `len` kept going to the real header through address live-ins computed before the loop. After the transfer the caller's list had a growing `len` over a data pointer that had been freed, which is where the wrapped values, zeros and faults came from.\n\nFix: an aggregate held by reference travels through the frame as the pointer itself (`frame_size_of` and `frame_align_of` give 8 for such a type); the Cranelift helper loads the pointer, the LLVM helper loads the pointer and, where a phi holds the struct by value, loads the value through it. The tier-0 writer stores each live-in as the value Cranelift holds, scalars and pointers alike. `the_osr_frame_lays_out_live_ins_at_natural_alignment` now pins the pointer layout.\n\nAlso: `ZYNTAX_DISABLE_OSR=1` on `TieredConfig::default()` to bisect a hot-loop miscompile without a rebuild.\n\nVerified: `list(range(n))` correct for n up to a million; ZynML nbody, nbody_ref, op_overload_ref and binary_trees with `--osr true` give their checksums.","files":null}]}